WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.992 line:90%
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.400 line:10%
 Hey, Lorraine Cink here
for the Women of Marvel.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.560 line:10%
And I am going to be talking
with the incredible Mary

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.260 line:10%
Livanos from Marvel
Studios, the director

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.800 line:10%
of production and development.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.600 line:90%
 Yes.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:15.400 line:90%
Hello.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.360 line:84%
 What does a director of
production and development

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.360 line:90%
do at Marvel Studios?

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.160 line:90%
 Sure.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.620 line:84%
 Because I've realized, you
know, a lot of our friends

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.830 line:84%
that are listening to this
are going to say, that's cool.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:25.760 line:90%
What is that?

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.690 line:90%
 It changes with every film.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:31.550 line:84%
But for Captain
Marvel it was my job

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.940 line:84%
to help make sure that
creatives, across the board

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.980 line:84%
in every department,
had all the tools

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.160 line:84%
and resources that they needed
in order to tell the story.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.580 line:84%
 So let's talk a little
bit about Captain Marvel.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.630 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.683 line:84%
 Now, you talked about
supporting the other, sort of--

00:00:47.683 --> 00:00:49.495 line:84%
- All the different departments.
- All the different departments.

00:00:49.495 --> 00:00:50.030 line:84%
 Yes.
Yes.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:52.850 line:84%
Providing key art from the
great Kelly Sue DeConnick

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:56.000 line:84%
runs and the early Captain
Marvel runs, to working very

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.817 line:90%
closely with the Air Force.

00:00:57.817 --> 00:00:59.150 line:84%
 You guys worked
with two different Air

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.390 line:84%
Force bases, correct?
- Yes.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.190 line:90%
Yes.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.350 line:84%
The film shot at
Edwards Air Force Base,

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:07.040 line:84%
but the bulk of our research
we conducted at Nellis Air

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.900 line:90%
Force Base with the 57th Wing.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.520 line:84%
Speaking with every
pilot that we could,

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.190 line:84%
getting inside their
heads, and they

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.430 line:84%
offered to fly Brie and Anna
Boden up in fighter jets.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.960 line:84%
And I said, haha,
you're kidding.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.370 line:90%
And they were not.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.450 line:90%
That was wild.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.910 line:84%
 So when you go back
and watch the film now--

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:26.030 line:84%
you've probably seen it a
lot more than most of us--

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:29.120 line:84%
what part, like, makes you feel
the most proud do you think?

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.430 line:84%
 There are a lot of parts
that made me very proud.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:32.930 line:90%
 I'll take them all.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.260 line:84%
 The message that Carol
Danvers didn't need fixing.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.060 line:90%
 Mm-hmm.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.400 line:84%
 That's what gives me chills
when I think about the movie.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.620 line:84%
 Yeah, the thing that always,
kind of, stuck with me is

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.000 line:84%
there's very much
a feeling of, like,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.550 line:90%
you are enough the way you are.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.620 line:84%
And that realization
that she sort of has.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.540 line:84%
 In a movie, a
character has problem,

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.760 line:84%
then, by the end of the movie,
you need to fix that problem.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.690 line:84%
Carol, it was the unexpected
discovery of that didn't

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:57.890 line:90%
necessarily need to happen.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.900 line:90%
And it was about self discovery.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.750 line:84%
Moments that make me
really, really happy,

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.150 line:84%
when Carol screams
back at the skrull.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.500 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.890 line:90%
 That feels so Carol.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:08.690 line:90%
I love Goose.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.070 line:90%
I love Goose so much.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.300 line:84%
 Oh, and I love that
Nick Fury is a cat man.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.100 line:90%
I just--

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.150 line:90%
[BOTH LAUGHING]

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.750 line:84%
It's just, like, a great fun
detail for the Marvel universe.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.110 line:84%
- Who would have thunk?
- Yeah.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.830 line:84%
Mary, thank you so much
for talking with us today.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.170 line:84%
 Thank you so
much for having me.

